{"availability":"available","full":"box/box-content-preview","name":"box-content-preview","description":"JavaScript library for rendering files stored on Box","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":120,"forks":137,"created":"2017-03-07T20:36:24Z","updated":"2026-10-09T21:02:42Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"https://developer.box.com/docs/box-content-preview","topics":["box-api","box-platform","javascript","preview","viewer"],"demo":"http://codepen.io/box-platform/pen/rmZdjm","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:54.526Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:54.526Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:54.526Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T23:11:54.526Z","stars":120,"forks":137}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The Box Content Preview library allows developers to easily embed high quality and interactive previews of Box files in desktop and mobile web applications. The JavaScript library fetches information about the file and its converted representations through the Box API, chooses the appropriate viewer for the file type, dynamically loads the necessary static assets and file representations, and finally renders the file. Box Content Preview also allows previews of multiple files to be loaded in the same container and exposes arrows to navigate between those files.","This library powers Preview in the main Box web application as well as the 'Get Embed Link' Box API endpoint."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/box/box-content-preview/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"d586b32cd17321f30d491ece8e0e902ad44d565ca6890ec2720201d07f15de86","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:54.692Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:54.692Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The Box Content Preview library allows developers to easily embed high quality and interactive previews of Box files in desktop and mobile web applications. The JavaScript library fetches information about the file and its converted representations through the Box API, chooses the appropriate viewer for the file type, dynamically loads the necessary static assets and file representations, and finally renders the file. Box Content Preview also allows previews of multiple files to be loaded in the same container and exposes arrows to navigate between those files.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/box/box-content-preview/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"The Box Content Preview library allows developers to easily embed high quality and interactive previews of Box files in desktop and mobile web applications. The JavaScript library fetches information about the file and its converted representations through the Box API, chooses the appropriate viewer for the file type, dynamically loads the necessary static assets and file…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/box/box-content-preview/blob/master/README.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"You can self-host the Box Content Preview library or reference the versions available on Box's CDN.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/box/box-content-preview/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"To self-host the Box Content Preview library, follow these steps:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/box/box-content-preview/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Box Content Preview needs an access token to make Box API calls.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/box/box-content-preview/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"If your application requires the end user to only be able to access a subset of the Content Preview functionality, you can use Token Exchange to appropriately downscope your App/Managed or Service Account token to a resulting token that has the desired set of permissions, and can thus, be securely passed to the end user client initializing the Content Preview.","sourc